{"version":"1","id":"f828c176-c10f-4598-b705-d712928068a1","handle":"dotnetsquad","name":".NET","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0ki3utHs--/f_auto/v1726216832/squads/f828c176-c10f-4598-b705-d712928068a1","description":null,"is_squad":true,"x":-8.9318,"y":10.3399,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":10,"newest_post_at":"2026-02-12T13:58:33.773Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-12-17T01:20:53.904Z","features":{"hype_score":0.05,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.2,"avg_read_time":1.9,"summary_length_avg":334.222222,"title_length_avg":39.5,"title_length_var":792.65,"tag_entropy":2.629936,"tag_diversity":1.9,"top_tag_share":0.2,"avg_upvotes":99.0,"median_upvotes":4.0,"avg_comments":11.5,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.117053,"zero_engagement_share":0.2,"viral_share":0.1,"posts_per_week":0.16567,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"recency_skew":0.428571},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[9.8676,8.7059],"cadence_depth":[-9.8382,-7.8235],"hype_variety":[8.25,-5.4265],"title_style":[9.7647,-1.7647]},"top_tags":[[".net",8],["c#",5],[".net-core",4],["webdev",3],["tech-news",2],["aspnet",2],["cloud",1],["microservices",1]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Do you store the JWT in localStorage, sessionStorage, Cookies? then this post is for you","Is dotnet still popularly used ??","What is .NET Core & Why it replaced .NET Framework?"],"outlier":["How To Use DeepSeek With .NET 9 | Hands-On With DeepSeek R1, Semantic Kernel & C#"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"KRXzNTmUH","title":"A Domain wrapper in C#","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-domain-wrapper-in-c--krxzntmuh","summary":"A C# library that enforces domain constraints at the type level, inspired by mathematical function domains. Instead of using primitive types like `int` or `string` with implicit validation scattered throughout code, it models values as belonging to explicitly defined mathematical sets (e.g., Age \u2208 [0, 120]). The approach centralizes validation logic, prevents invalid states from existing, and enables functional composition through Map/Bind operations. The library separates domain definitions from values and policies, making constraints structural rather than optional.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--Mto2SB5k--/f_auto/v1770904715/posts/KRXzNTmUH?_a=BAMAMiiu0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-12T13:58:33.773Z"},{"id":"U8Pr1Ph5t","title":">WPF still live","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/wpf-still-live-u8pr1ph5t","summary":"A newcomer to development asks the community whether WPF (Windows Presentation Foundation) is still actively evolving and has market demand, or if they should invest time learning a different technology stack instead.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--cn2u0Lb0--/f_auto/v1767361248/posts/U8Pr1Ph5t?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2026-01-02T13:40:48.055Z"},{"id":"zJ84ZLTQJ","title":"What is .NET Core & Why it replaced .NET Framework?","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-net-core-why-it-replaced-net-framework--zj84zltqj","summary":".NET Core replaced .NET Framework to address modern development needs. While .NET Framework was Windows-only, tightly coupled to IIS, and slow to innovate, .NET Core introduced cross-platform support (Windows, Linux, macOS), high performance, open-source licensing, and cloud/container-friendly architecture. Microsoft strategically shifted all future development to .NET Core (now unified as .NET 5+), leaving .NET Framework in maintenance-only mode for legacy enterprise systems. For modern APIs, microservices, or cloud applications, current .NET versions (8, 9, 10) are the recommended choice.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--IyJO5NCb--/f_auto/v1766984725/posts/zJ84ZLTQJ?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-29T05:01:17.805Z"},{"id":"K4L53Quxb","title":"Build a Raspberry Pi kiosk with Avalonia UI and DotNetBrowser!","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-a-raspberry-pi-kiosk-with-avalonia-ui-and-dotnetbrowser--k4l53quxb","summary":"A guide demonstrates how to build a kiosk application on Raspberry Pi using Avalonia UI framework and DotNetBrowser. The approach runs outside the desktop environment, offering developers more flexibility than traditional lockdown browsers while combining native app capabilities with web development simplicity.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZiN9H31S--/f_auto/v1762775083/posts/K4L53Quxb?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-10T11:44:40.154Z"},{"id":"2yoL7r91m","title":"Do you store the JWT in localStorage, sessionStorage, Cookies? then this post is for you","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/do-you-store-the-jwt-in-localstorage-sessionstorage-cookies-then-this-post-is-for-you-2yol7r91m","summary":"Storing JWTs in vulnerable client-side storage (like localStorage, sessionStorage, or cookies) can expose applications to significant security risks. Alternatives include using in-memory storage and implementing a refresh token mechanism. This allows users to maintain their sessions without re-authenticating upon page reloads while mitigating potential attacks. Setting cookies with httpOnly, Secure, and SameSite flags is crucial for security. A short-lived JWT with periodic refreshing enhances protection.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--frEj4WS5--/f_auto/v1740537395/posts/2yoL7r91m","num_upvotes":949,"num_comments":99,"created_at":"2025-02-26T02:36:34.852Z"},{"id":"cNH7DTCW3","title":"New Member of .NET Community","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-member-of-net-community-cnh7dtcw3","summary":"A .NET developer new to the platform is focusing on migrating ASP.NET Web Forms applications to Blazor, using different render modes depending on the application. They are seeking to learn from the community.","image":null,"num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-21T14:36:54.838Z"},{"id":"ZXwojIQeE","title":"\ud83d\ude07","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/zxwojiqee","summary":"Expressing enthusiasm for being part of the .Net developer community, and likely highlighting the benefits and opportunities that come with it.","image":null,"num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-06T04:41:35.886Z"},{"id":"0SlibSwAF","title":"How To Use DeepSeek With .NET 9 | Hands-On With DeepSeek R1, Semantic Kernel & C#","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-use-deepseek-with-net-9-hands-on-with-deepseek-r1-semantic-kernel-c--0slibswaf","summary":null,"image":null,"num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-02-04T08:07:40.546Z"},{"id":"JtsL6hNUV","title":"Is dotnet still popularly used ??","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/is-dotnet-still-popularly-used--jtsl6hnuv","summary":"Despite enjoying dotnet training and acknowledging its new features and cross-platform capabilities, concerns remain about its steady growth and the willingness of new companies to adopt it.","image":null,"num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2024-12-27T09:13:09.736Z"},{"id":"6bZR33CIH","title":"Need an Advice","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/need-an-advice-6bzr33cih","summary":"The writer is seeking advice on whether to start learning C# and .NET 6 as recommended by a video they watched, or if they should consider .NET 8. They mention a book recommendation, 'Pro C# 10 with .NET 6', and are confused about which version to focus on.","image":null,"num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2024-12-17T01:20:53.904Z"}],"similar_handles":["nuxtandvue","watercooler","allfrontend","dfa0u7-fs","horde"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"a41f99d2-8439-4100-a646-848ba12512f6","handle":"nuxtandvue","name":"Vu